<\body>
  <doc-data|<doc-title|A Constructive Introduction to Quantum Field
  Theory>|<doc-subtitle|Lecture 3: Stochastic quantisation and stochastic
  observables>|<doc-author|<author-data|<author-name|M.
  Gubinelli>|<author-affiliation|Mathematical Institute, University of
  Oxford>>>|<doc-date|SISSA, October 2026>>

  <abstract-data|<\abstract>
    We first show that the Gaussian free field is the stationary one-time
    (resp. one-point) marginal of the parabolic (resp. elliptic) stochastic
    quantisation equation. We then decompose it along a scale parameter and
    take as primary objects the <em|stochastic observables>: martingales in
    the filtration of finite-resolution measurements. As examples we study
    Wick powers as observables in every dimension, and their products
    (operator product expansion). Interactions are introduced in Lecture 4.
    Exercises are collected at the end of each section. These notes follow
    the slides of Lecture 3.
  </abstract>>

